<div class="quick-facts">
  <div class="fact-card"><span class="fact-icon">🏛️</span><span class="fact-label">Capital</span><span class="fact-value"><a href="/capital-of-australia/">Canberra</a></span></div>
  <div class="fact-card"><span class="fact-icon">💰</span><span class="fact-label">Currency</span><span class="fact-value"><a href="/currency-in-australia/">Australian dollar ($)</a></span></div>
  <div class="fact-card"><span class="fact-icon">🗣️</span><span class="fact-label">Language</span><span class="fact-value"><a href="/language-of-australia/">English</a></span></div>
  <div class="fact-card"><span class="fact-icon">📞</span><span class="fact-label">Dialling Code</span><span class="fact-value"><a href="/dialling-code-for-australia/">+61</a></span></div>
  <div class="fact-card"><span class="fact-icon">🌍</span><span class="fact-label">Region</span><span class="fact-value">Australia and New Zealand</span></div>
  <div class="fact-card"><span class="fact-icon">👥</span><span class="fact-label">Population</span><span class="fact-value"><a href="/population-of-australia/">27,536,874</a></span></div>
</div>

<p class="country-intro">Australia is the only country that is also a continent, known for the Great Barrier Reef, the Outback and its unique wildlife. Australia is located in Australia and New Zealand and has a population of around 27.5 million. Its capital city is Canberra, and the most widely spoken official language is English. As an island nation, Australia has no land borders.</p>
<p>By the numbers, Australia is the 54th most populous of the 196 countries covered on this site, home to 0.34% of the world&#39;s population. By land area it ranks 6th out of 196, with a population density of roughly 4 people per km².</p>
<p class="last-verified">Facts last checked 16 September 2026.</p>

<div class="ad-slot"></div>

<h2>Australia — key facts at a glance</h2>
<div class="table-scroll">
<table class="facts-table">
